    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the clear engine of the offense. With an elite efficiency score of 83.29, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park factor boost and favorable hitting conditions against Hancock. While the opposing pitcher\u2019s ability to control the running game forces a slight reduction in his stolen base potential, his position in the two-hole and raw talent make him the highest-floor play in the lineup. **Jackson Merrill** also provides a strong start (60.85), as his matchup against the weaker Abbott presents an ideal scenario for high-leverage counting stats, successfully offsetting the minor penalty incurred from the platoon disadvantage.\n\nThe optimizer faced a narrow margin regarding the final middle infield and utility spots, particularly with **Brayan Rocchio** lingering on the bench. **Brayan Rocchio** recorded a 40.07 score\u2014nearly mirroring **Nasim Nunez**\u2014but was ultimately sidelined due to a lower projected batting average contribution and a suboptimal spot at the bottom of the order. Conversely, **Nasim Nunez** and **Coby Mayo** remain in the starting lineup to capitalize on their respective platoon dynamics, though both carry risk due to facing the formidable Webb, whose 3.46 xERA acts as a significant drag on their offensive potential. \n\nManagement is keeping a close watch on **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who are both facing high-end arms. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.90) is pushed into the lineup by his high-order placement and platoon advantage, but his score is tempered by the elite 2.74 xERA of S\u00e1nchez. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** maintains a respectable 57.47, sustained largely by his favorable role as the number two hitter. Owners should note that with **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remaining on the IL, our depth is being tested; expect increased usage of **Brayan Rocchio** and **Heliot Ramos** in the coming week if the current starters struggle to overcome these difficult pitching matchups.",
